import ../../helpers/driver.dl

appearance above appearance:
    height is 260
appearance stage appearance:
    height is 120
appearance below appearance:
    height is 300

document canvas visibility:
    region "Above" using above appearance:
    surface "Canvas" using stage appearance
    region "Below" using below appearance:

to [paint a visibility probe] {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    increment the value at (painting's instance's state as a pointer to integer)
    animate UI view (painting's frame's view)

set calls to 0
set instance to an instance of canvas visibility with state (the address of calls)
set window to the address of instance
bind (the control labeled "Canvas" in window) in window to (the function named "paint a visibility probe $") for event 1
set view to a UI view of window sized 300 by 200 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
# Keep hover transitions independent of the canvas's animation scheduling.
set view's cursor to a UI point at 290.0 and 190.0
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (calls = 0) reporting "An offscreen canvas ran its paint callback"
set view's layout's scroll position and view's layout's scroll target to 250.0
request a UI redraw in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (calls = 1) reporting "A visible canvas did not run its paint callback"
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (calls = 2) reporting "A visible canvas could not continue its animation"
set view's layout's scroll position and view's layout's scroll target to 300.0
request a UI redraw in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (calls = 3) reporting "A partially visible canvas stopped painting"
set view's layout's scroll position and view's layout's scroll target to 400.0
request a UI redraw in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (calls = 3) reporting "Scrolling a canvas out of view retained its paint callback"
set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
set paints to surface's paints
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (surface's paints = paints) reporting "An offscreen canvas kept its view repainting"
close the address of view
close window
print line "Canvas callbacks animate while visible and stop when scrolled out of view."
